					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-11-08 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br><img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2215/1885010567_d55135b85d.jpg" alt="" width="500" height="375" /><br /><br />Shout out to The Smoking Section for the <strong><a href="http://smokingsection.rawkus.com/TSS/?p=2289#more-2289">review</a></strong> of last week&#39;s Red Bull Big Tune battle! Congrats to Sabzi for takin&#39; home the crown.....<br /><br />Peace<br />daps1<br /><br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-11-06 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br><font size="2">i&#39;m in San Francisco getting ready for these shows with Nefasha Ayer... check it out! -- gtzi http://www.myspace.com/nefashaayer<br /><br />The Red Poppy Art House Presents:<br /><br />NEFASHA AYER: Excerpts from the Space of In-between<br />Two nights! Friday, November 9th and Saturday, November 10th<br /><br />Drawing
inspiration from jazz, blues and traditional Ethiopian melodies and
rhythms, Nefasha Ayer (loosely translated from Amharic as &ldquo;the wind
that travels&rdquo;) is an in-progress body of music exploring the most
essential qualities shared among individuals worldwide whose identity
no longer fits within the boundaries of one country, culture or
tradition. Through its tones and colors, poetic texts and
trans-cultural melodic scores, Nefasha Ayer joins the continents of
Africa, South Asia and America to produce a uniquely San Franciscan
music, born from present-day realities of life at the crossroads.<br /><br />This
weekend&rsquo;s shows feature in-progress selections from Nefasha Ayer, with
Ethiopian-born vocalist and Art House Director Meklit Hadero, Art House
Founder/Director and guitarist Todd T. Brown, Carnatic saxophonist
Prasant Radhakrishnan (of VidyA), award-winning poet Michael Warr,
Ethiopian MC Gabriel Teodros (of Abyssinian Creole), bassist/flautist
Eliyahu Sills (of Qadim), and percussionist Mohini Rustagi (of Ambika).
On Friday night, we&#39;ll be joined by bassist Miles Jay (formerly of
Yousou N&#39;Dour).<br /><br />In April, the Red Poppy Art House received a
grant from the San Francisco Foundation and the Fund for Artists
commissioning this work.<br /><br /><br />For more information: www.redpoppyarthouse.org/concerts<br /><br />$15 suggested donation. Friday and Saturday: Doors open at 7:30 pm. Show at 8:00 pm.<br /><br />Red Poppy Art House<br />2698 Folsom St @ 23rd<br />San Francisco, CA 94110<br />www.redpoppyarthouse.org</font><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-11-05 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><div align="center"><strong><u><span style="font-size: larger">FCC Hearing on Media Ownership this Friday!!</span> </u></strong><br /></div><br /><br />

<ul><li class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial">The FCC is getting ready to give Big Media
     corporations even more control over what we see and hear.</span></strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial"> </span></li><li class="MsoNormal"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial">The FCC&#39;s final <a href="http://www.reclaimthemedia.org/legislation_and_regulation/fcc_announces_final_media_owne=5565" target="_blank"><strong>official public hearing</strong></a><strong> </strong>will be <strong>Friday
     Nov 9, at <a href="http://www.townhallseattle.org/" target="_blank">Town
     Hall Seattle</a>. </strong></span></li><li class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial">This is the big one</span></strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial"> - <strong>We can stop the FCC in
     its tracks</strong> by showing up in force this Friday and speaking out for
     diverse and locally accountable media.<strong> </strong></span></li><li class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial"><a href="http://www.reclaimthemedia.org/" target="_blank">Reclaim the Media</a> is running workshops</span></strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial"> all week for folks who want to
     testify. </span></li></ul>

<p class="MsoNormal"><strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial">What&#39;s
happening and what&#39;s at stake?<br />
<br />
</span></strong><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Arial">The FCC is about to
rewrite the federal media ownership rules to give more power to Big Media
companies like Clear Channel and Murdoch&#39;s News Corp. FCC Chairman Kevin Martin
even wants <strong>to allow a single company to combine local newspaper, TV and
radio stations under one roof - and under single editorial control. 
<!--
